fix(cors): allow Pages preview deployments, and use the stable Pages URL

Two problems with the allowlist as deployed.

ALLOWED_ORIGINS held "https://b7907c2a.taktouka.pages.dev.pages.dev" --
the suffix was doubled, so the host did not resolve and the browser was
refused on every request. It also named a per-deployment URL, whose hash
changes on every push, rather than the stable one.

Fixed to https://taktouka.pages.dev, and the origin check now accepts
any subdomain of a .pages.dev host already on the list. Without that,
every preview deployment fails CORS while looking identical to
production, because its hash can never be in an exact-match list.

The expansion is restricted to .pages.dev entries deliberately. Applying
it to an arbitrary allowed origin would be a real hole -- anyone holding
a subdomain of it would inherit API access -- whereas a subdomain of our
own Pages project can only be another deployment of this project.
Verified against seven cases, including https://taktouka.pages.dev.evil.com
and https://nottaktouka.pages.dev, both correctly denied.

README now points at the live deployment and records the measured
numbers on both sides of the move: 42s first load on the old container,
about 20 ms Worker startup now.

Root package-lock.json is committed so the Pages build resolves the same
tree every time.
